IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`
IMPORT `vmu-s08-construction`
IMPORT `vmu-s09-regulations`
IMPORT `vmu-s10-notification`

-- Tests of sections 8, 9 and 10.
-- Each expected value is worked out by hand from the quoted line above it.

§ `Section 8 -- Certain monetary amounts to be construed in fee units or penalty units`

-- src:80 | (1) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
-- "A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed": all three facts.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Leaving out any one of the three, the text says neither yes nor no.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:82 | (1A) A provision in an Act or a statutory rule authorising an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the instrument maker to make a legislative instrument to prescribe, fix or charge that fee by reference to a fee unit.
-- "A provision in an Act or a statutory rule authorising an instrument maker to make a legislative instrument that prescribes, fixes or charges a fee (however expressed) may be construed".
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `an Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `a statutory rule` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A provision in a legislative instrument, or in an instrument of another kind, is not within the description.
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `a legislative instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `an instrument of another kind` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Leaving out either of the other two facts.
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `an Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1A) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a legislative instrument that fixes the fee by reference to a fee unit` `an Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:83 | (2) A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule (however expressed) may be construed as authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule to prescribe that penalty by reference to a penalty unit.
-- "A provision in an Act authorising the Governor in Council to make a statutory rule that prescribes a penalty for an offence against the statutory rule (however expressed) may be construed".
#ASSERT `s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) -- the provision may be construed as authorising a statutory rule that fixes the penalty by reference to a penalty unit` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 9 -- Regulations`

-- src:86 | (1) The Governor in Council, on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer, may make regulations amending any statutory rule made under any Act to—
-- "The Governor in Council, on the certificate and recommendation of the Treasurer, may make regulations amending any statutory rule made under any Act to—": each of the seven purposes (a) to (g).
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount calculated in accordance with the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting fee units to fees in monetary amounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `converting penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `increasing fees in monetary amounts by the cumulative annual rates` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A purpose that the paragraphs do not list, or a regulation without the certificate and recommendation, or one that does not amend a statutory rule: no answer.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE TRUE `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` FALSE TRUE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) -- the regulation may be made` TRUE FALSE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- "(a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)— (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, ... dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, ... by the value of a fee unit".
-- On 1 July 2004 itself and on 30 June 2004 the divisor is 10 dollars; on 2 July 2004 it is the value of a fee unit.
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 30 6 2004) `dividing the fee by 10 dollars`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the fee by 10 dollars`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the fee by 10 dollars`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- "(b) ... (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, ... dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, ... by the value of a penalty unit".
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 30 6 2004) `dividing the penalty by 100 dollars`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the penalty by 100 dollars`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the penalty by 100 dollars`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
-- A fee conversion is not a penalty conversion, whatever the day.
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`

-- src:101 | (c) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit under this Act;
-- src:102 | (d) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(c), the regulation converts penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:103 | (e) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(d), the regulation converts the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit specified or referred to in the statutory rule to the equivalent monetary amount of that fee unit or penalty unit under this Act;
-- src:104 | (f) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(e), the regulation converts fee units to fees in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:105 | (g) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(f), the regulation converts penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts by multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- src:106 | (h) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(g), the regulation increases any fees that are less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
-- Paragraphs (c) and (d) both name a regulation under subsection (1)(c), one for fee units and one for penalty units; (e), (f), (g), (h) follow, one for each of (1)(d), (e), (f), (g).
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act` (Date 1 1 2010) `converting fee units to the equivalent number of fee units having regard to the current value of a fee unit`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act` (Date 1 1 2010) `converting penalty units to the equivalent number of penalty units having regard to the current value of a penalty unit`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fee units or penalty units to fee units or penalty units calculated in accordance with the Act` (Date 1 1 2010) `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount under the Act`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount calculated in accordance with the Act` (Date 1 1 2010) `converting the monetary amount of a fee unit or penalty unit to the equivalent monetary amount under the Act`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fee units to fees in monetary amounts` (Date 1 1 2010) `multiplying the amount of the fee unit by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting fee units to fees in monetary amounts` (Date 1 1 2010) `multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `converting penalty units to penalties in monetary amounts` (Date 1 1 2010) `multiplying the amount of the penalty unit by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`
#ASSERT     `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `increasing fees in monetary amounts by the cumulative annual rates` (Date 1 1 2010) `increasing fees less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `increasing fees in monetary amounts by the cumulative annual rates` (Date 1 1 2010) `some other conversion`
#ASSERT NOT `s 9(2) -- the conversion certified is the one that the subsection names for the regulation` `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` (Date 1 1 2010) `some other conversion`

-- src:95 | (a) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(a)—
-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- Paragraph (a) as a calculation: a fee of 125 dollars is 12.5 fee units on or before 1 July 2004 (125 / 10); after it, 125 / 12.5 = 10 fee units at a value of 12.5.
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` 125 (Date 30 6 2004) 12.5 EQUALS JUST 12.5
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` 125 (Date 1 7 2004) 12.5 EQUALS JUST 12.5
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` 125 (Date 2 7 2004) 12.5 EQUALS JUST 10
-- A value of 0 divides nothing: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(a) -- the number of fee units to which the regulation converts the fee` 125 (Date 2 7 2004) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:98 | (b) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(b)—
-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
-- Paragraph (b) as a calculation: a penalty of 250 dollars is 2.5 penalty units on or before 1 July 2004 (250 / 100); after it, 250 / 125 = 2 penalty units at a value of 125.
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the number of penalty units to which the regulation converts the penalty` 250 (Date 1 7 2004) 125 EQUALS JUST 2.5
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the number of penalty units to which the regulation converts the penalty` 250 (Date 2 7 2004) 125 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `s 9(2)(b) -- the number of penalty units to which the regulation converts the penalty` 250 (Date 2 7 2004) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:94 | (2) Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—
-- "Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 does not apply to a regulation made under this section if the Treasurer certifies in writing that—".
-- Certified in writing, with the conversion that paragraph (a)(i) names for a regulation taking effect on 1 July 2004.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` TRUE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the fee by 10 dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not certified in writing: the condition is not met.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` FALSE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the fee by 10 dollars` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Certified in writing, but with the conversion of paragraph (a)(ii) for a regulation taking effect on 1 July 2004: not the one the subsection names.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` TRUE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 1 7 2004) `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day after: the conversion of paragraph (a)(ii) is the one named.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` TRUE `converting fees in monetary amounts to fee units` (Date 2 7 2004) `dividing the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A purpose that paragraphs (a) to (g) of subsection (1) do not list: not a regulation made under this section, so the text does not say, whatever the certificate.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` TRUE `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` (Date 2 7 2004) `some other conversion` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(2) -- this subsection disapplies Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994 to the regulation` FALSE `a purpose not listed in section 9(1)` (Date 2 7 2004) `some other conversion` EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:107 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(a) and (b), in calculating the number of fee units or penalty units, the number of fee units or penalty units is deemed to be calculated in accordance with those provisions if the fee unit or penalty unit is rounded up to the next 2 decimal places.
-- "rounded up to the next 2 decimal places": a number calculated as 3.456 is deemed calculated in accordance with (a) or (b) when stated as 3.46.
#ASSERT `s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` 3.456 3.46 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Stated as 3.45 (rounded down), or as 3.456 (not rounded): this subsection does not deem it.
#ASSERT `s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` 3.456 3.45 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` 3.456 3.456 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A number with 2 decimal places is its own rounding up; 3.4601 rounds up to 3.47.
#ASSERT `s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` 2.5 2.5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(3) -- the number of units the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(a) or (b)` 3.4601 3.47 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- src:108 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2)(f), in calculating the amount of a fee, the amount of the fee is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the fee is rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
-- "rounded to the nearest 10 cents": a fee calculated as 43.855 is deemed in accordance when stated as 43.90, and not when stated as 43.80.
#ASSERT `s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(f)` 43.855 43.9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(f)` 43.855 43.8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Calculated as 43.85, exactly half way between 43.80 and 43.90: NOTHING whichever is stated.
#ASSERT `s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(f)` 43.85 43.9 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(f)` 43.85 43.8 EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:109 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(g), in calculating the amount of a penalty, the amount of the penalty is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar.
-- "rounded to the nearest dollar": a penalty calculated as 281.68 is deemed in accordance when stated as 282, and not when stated as 281.
#ASSERT `s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(g)` 281.68 282 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(g)` 281.68 281 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Calculated as 281.5, exactly half way: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty the regulation states is deemed to be calculated in accordance with section 9(2)(g)` 281.5 282 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 10 -- Notification of fees and penalties`

-- src:113 | (1) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees and penalties calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee or penalty.
-- "The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule that provides for fees or penalties by fee units or penalty units must take reasonable steps".
-- Arguments in order: the instrument; it provides for fees or penalties by units; the person is the Minister responsible for administering it.
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `an Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `a statutory rule` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A legislative instrument is not named in subsection (1): no answer. Nor is any other kind.
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `a legislative instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `an instrument of another kind` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An Act that does not provide for fees or penalties by units, or a person who is not the responsible Minister: no answer.
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `an Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts is given` `an Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where the duty arises, it is met if reasonable steps were taken (the last argument).
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `an Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `an Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(1) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `a legislative instrument` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:115 | (2) The Minister responsible for administering an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of those fees calculated in accordance with section 7 are notified to the public generally or to the sector of the public likely to be affected by the fee.
-- "an Act or a statutory rule under which a legislative instrument is made that provides for fees by fee units": fees only; the duty is the same.
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `an Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `a statutory rule` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `a legislative instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `an Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister must take reasonable steps to ensure that notice of the monetary amounts of the fees is given` `an Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `an Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `a statutory rule` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 10(2) -- the Minister has taken the steps that the subsection requires` `an Act` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
